      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-15-3",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Beholding evil and good alike. First principle: total surveillance is God's attribute — no deed escapes the watching eyes that Hebrews says are open before Him with whom we have to do.",
      "density": 2.3429,
      "words": 32,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 27,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-10-12",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Hatred stirs; love covers. First principle: the covering verb returns in the New Testament — Peter and James both quote it; charity is the sin-hiding blanket, judgment the stirrer.",
      "density": 2.1536,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 25,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-8-23",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Wisdom antedates the earth. First principle: from everlasting — the attribute of God alone, here the speech of Wisdom; the fathers read it of the Son's eternal generation.",
      "density": 2.0714,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-26-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The fool's folly-repeat. First principle: relapse without re-creation is the warning — Peter quotes the dog and adds the washed sow; nature, not habit, is the problem.",
      "density": 2.0464,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 24,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-3-5",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Lean not on your own understanding. First principle: the heart-lean is the whole matter — trust is total or it is not trust; self-understanding is the rival crutch.",
      "density": 1.9571,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-27-19",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The heart reflects the heart. First principle: self-knowledge is mirror-knowledge — what you see in others is your own heart's reflection; the proverb is a standing audit.",
      "density": 1.9321,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 22,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-31-28",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The virtuous woman praised by children and husband. First principle: the crowning praise is spoken by family — the fear-of-the-LORD woman outlasts charm and beauty in her children's mouths.",
      "density": 1.925,
      "words": 29,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 21,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-30-5",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "A shield to all who trust; add not to His words. First principle: purity of the Word and prohibition of addition bracket the verse — Revelation's ending and Deuteronomy's warning agree.",
      "density": 1.9179,
      "words": 31,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-25-21",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Feed the enemy; give the thirsty water. First principle: the enemy-feeding command is the Old Testament root of love-your-enemies — Paul quotes it to make coals-of-fire kindness.",
      "density": 1.8179,
      "words": 27,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-17-17",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "A brother born for adversity. First principle: friendship's test is timing — all times and adversities; the greater-than-Solomon laid down His life for His friends.",
      "density": 1.7679,
      "words": 25,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-17-15",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Both verdict-errors are abomination. First principle: the courtroom abomination makes the gospel startling — God justifies the ungodly while remaining just, through the propitiation.",
      "density": 1.7429,
      "words": 24,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-30-8",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Agur's proportioned bread prayer. First principle: the middle-way petition — full self-sufficiency denies God, destitution denies His name; convenient food is the requested mean.",
      "density": 1.7429,
      "words": 24,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 20,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-22-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Old-age constancy promised to early training. First principle: formation is directional — the shaped path shapes the walker; Ephesians charges fathers with the same nurture.",
      "density": 1.7107,
      "words": 25,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-21-1",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Turned like rivers of water whithersoever He will. First principle: rulers are reroutable — Ezra, Daniel, and Cyrus all prove the redirecting hand over imperial decisions.",
      "density": 1.6786,
      "words": 26,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-11-31",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "If the righteous are recompensed here, how much more the wicked. First principle: judgment begins with the house — Peter quotes the much-more logic of the sinner's fate.",
      "density": 1.6714,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-31-6",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Wine for the heavy-hearted dying — a mercy-analgesic, not a lifestyle. First principle: the proverb prescribes numbness only for the perishing, implicitly forbidding it for judges and kings.",
      "density": 1.6714,
      "words": 28,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-3-34",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Scorners scorned; lowly graced. First principle: the grace-gradient proverb — James and Peter both quote it verbatim to install humility as the grace-receiver.",
      "density": 1.6607,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 19,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-24-24",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The people curse the moral flip. First principle: calling wickedness righteous draws national curse — the proverb is the public's own verdict on verdict-benders.",
      "density": 1.6286,
      "words": 24,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-20-9",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The rhetorical impossibility of self-purification. First principle: no one can say it — the heart-cleaning requires a Heart-maker; 1 John names the self-deceiver.",
      "density": 1.6036,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 18,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-29-18",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Law-keeping is the happy alternative to unrestraint. First principle: without revealed vision, self-rule kills — Judges' refrain and Isaiah's sheep-stray are the same diagnosis.",
      "density": 1.5714,
      "words": 24,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-3-11",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Correction is sonship-proof; weariness is forbidden. First principle: Hebrews quotes this twice to reframe suffering — the chastened child is the legitimate child.",
      "density": 1.5464,
      "words": 23,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 17,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-21-3",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "Justice outweighs altar-traffic. First principle: the mercy-over-sacrifice proverb — Samuel, Isaiah, Hosea, and Jesus all carry the same scale.",
      "density": 1.3893,
      "words": 19,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 16,
      "gate": "PASS",
      "violations": [],
      "context": {
        "citations": []
      }
    },
    {
      "entryId": "pro-20-20",
      "file": "bookThreadDetails",
      "field": "principle",
      "text": "The lamp extinguished in obscure darkness. First principle: parental contempt extinguishes light — Exodus' death-penalty command becomes the lamp-out image.",
      "density": 1.3,
      "words": 20,
      "sentences": 2,
      "maxSentenceWords": 14,
      "gate": "PASS",
